#: src/finding-navigating.md:3
msgid "Finding & Navigating"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed provides several ways to move around your codebase quickly. Here's an "
"overview of the main navigation tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:7 src/finding-navigating.md:48
msgid "Command Palette"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:9
msgid ""
"The Command Palette (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-p\\|ctrl-shift-p</"
"kbd>) is your gateway to almost everything in Zed. Type a few characters to "
"filter commands, then press Enter to execute."
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:11
msgid "[Learn more about the Command Palette →](./command-palette.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:13
msgid "File Finder"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:15
msgid ""
"Open any file in your project with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-p\\|ctrl-p</"
"kbd>. Type part of the filename or path to narrow results."
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:17
msgid "Project Search"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:19
msgid ""
"Search across all files with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-h\\|ctrl-"
"shift-h</kbd>. Start typing in the search field to begin searching—results "
"appear as you type."
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:21
msgid ""
"Results appear in a [multibuffer](./multibuffers.md), letting you edit "
"matches in place."
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:23
msgid "Go to Definition"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:25
msgid ""
"Jump to where a symbol is defined with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">f12\\|f12</"
"kbd> (or `Cmd+Click` / `Ctrl+Click`). If there are multiple definitions, "
"they open in a multibuffer."
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:27
msgid "Go to Symbol"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:29
msgid ""
"**Current file:** <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-o\\|ctrl-shift-o</kbd> "
"opens an outline of symbols in the active file"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:30
msgid ""
"**Entire project:** <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-t\\|ctrl-t</kbd> searches "
"symbols across all files"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:32 src/finding-navigating.md:55
msgid "Outline Panel"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:34
msgid ""
"The Outline Panel (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-b\\|ctrl-shift-b</"
"kbd>) shows a persistent tree view of symbols in the current file. It's "
"especially useful with [multibuffers](./multibuffers.md) for navigating "
"search results or diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:36
msgid "[Learn more about the Outline Panel →](./outline-panel.md)"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:38 src/finding-navigating.md:56
msgid "Tab Switcher"
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:40
msgid ""
"Quickly switch between open tabs with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-tab\\|"
"ctrl-tab</kbd>. Tabs are sorted by recent use—keep holding Ctrl and press "
"Tab to cycle through them."
msgstr ""

#: src/finding-navigating.md:42
msgid "[Learn more about the Tab Switcher →](./tab-switcher.md)"
msgstr ""

